// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
// specs/t27f/lukomorye_graph_terminal.t27 -- T27V Lukomorye: the ONE canonical work graph drawn as an
// oak. Wave A: the contract (layout, growth order, camera, admission, provenance, honesty), no renderer.
// Refs gHashTag/t27#12779 (live work graph), see #10034 (T27F) and the reuse list below.
//
// WHY: the owner's V7 order: one graph, one deterministic tree layout of it, one native window.
//   roots   = t27 language levels (NX_ROOT) and the specs that hang from them (NK_SPEC)
//   trunk   = the t27b pipeline (NX_TRUNK)
//   branch  = an epic (NX_EPIC)
//   twig    = an issue (NX_ISSUE); an artifact that is not verified yet is a BUD on the twig layer
//   leaf    = a verified artifact or mesh (work_graph_ext.t27 wx_artifact_verified), nothing else
//   space   = agents, tasks, actions, releases: the T27L feed, the live feed, THREAD-VISION
// The graph is work_graph.t27's WorkGraph with the kinds of work_graph_ext.t27; this file adds no
// node, no edge and no kind of its own. BELONGS_TO is the canonical tree edge; HAS_CHILD is derived
// (wx_child_count / wx_child_at), never stored. The layout picks the FIRST BELONGS_TO out of a node as
// its tree parent; every other edge -- a second parent, a DEPENDS_ON cycle, a VERIFIES -- stays in the
// graph and is counted as a cross edge (tree_edges + cross_edges == edges): nothing is discarded to
// force a tree shape.
//
// THE PIECES, all integer, no division by a value the caller controls:
//   layout      lk_layout: a layer per node from its kind; within a layer the order is (rank of the
//               tree parent when the parent sits on a lower layer, else last; then node index). x is
//               symmetric slot spacing (SPACE_3), y is layer * 3 * SPACE_4 (vf_style.t27). Same graph,
//               same layout, every time: no clock, no randomness, no hash order.
//   growth      roots -> trunk -> branches -> twigs -> leaves -> space: the layout order IS the
//               growth order, acts 1..6 (lk_act_of). Offline is a replay of the same order.
//   camera      six frames of ONE view (ground, axo-l, axo-r, plan, front, side): lk_fit fits the
//               layout's box into the field; lk_cam_should_move is the hysteresis (5 percent zoom
//               change, 500 ms stable, 1000 ms cooldown; a critical user action bypasses it). Elapsed
//               times are inputs from the monotonic clock (t27t.t27), never a wall clock.
//   admission   at most 1000 nodes and 5000 edges; an event grows the graph by at most 5 nodes and 4
//               edges (apply_event's widest cases, the offer and the result), so an event is refused
//               whole -- never applied in part -- when it could pass a budget, and goes to a durable
//               dead letter (t27m.t27 reason overflow, class transient). The alert is t27m's 80 percent.
//   provenance  a bridge artifact carries t27r.t27's fact state: verified -> EXACT node and edges,
//               unverified -> SUGGESTED edges and an UNKNOWN node, disputed -> UNKNOWN edges. Only the
//               verified one makes a leaf; a later verification adds the EXACT edge and keeps the old.
//   honesty     the source of what is drawn is NONE, FIXTURE, REPLAY or LIVE; only LIVE wears the live
//               badge, NONE is an honest empty state, a fixture is never drawn as live.
//   passes      ink before color: the color pass is refused until the ink pass is done.
//   events      the 20 actions 137..156 of t27l.t27 (surface "visual"); there is no view_switched.
//
// REUSED (what each gives, nothing duplicated): #12779 the work graph and its feed (work_graph.t27);
// #10034 T27F (spec_graph labels); #10537 / #10259 / #11385 / #12884 / #13131 are earlier homes of
// the board, window, actor feed and scene work (titles checked 2026-11-08); their read-through is a
// Wave B item (BLOCKERS of the report). The order also named #6198 (t27b port epic), #11509 (the
// three-computer mesh) and #6655 (Verified Compute PoC, closed): checked 2026-11-08, none of them is
// board, window, feed or scene work, so nothing here rests on them.
// NOT CLAIMED: no window, no renderer, no t27b build (Waves B-E); the palette is NOT defined here --
// the V7 ink (red #e43a33 -> purple #7c22a0) and color (browns, greens, dark blue) conflict with the
// black-and-white T27F style of vf_style.t27, so the palette is an owner decision before Wave B and
// gets one home (vf_style.t27), not a second one here. The research citations of the order are
// unverified candidates, not facts. This contract's tests have not been run (swap gate BLOCKED).
// phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module T27fLukomoryeGraphTerminal;

